We investigate the existence and distinctness of positive solutions to a family of frameworks, which are represented by the equation \begin{equation}\label{eq1}
\left\{
\begin{array}{lr}
\mathrm{div}\left(\left| \nabla u\right|^{p-2}+\mu\left| \nabla
u\right|^{\alpha-1}\right)\nu=0\quad\mbox{in } \Omega\setminus
\Omega_{\mu},\\
\mathrm{div}\left(\left| \nabla u\right|^{p-2}\right)=0\quad\mbox{in }
\Omega_{\mu},\\
u=0\quad\mbox{on }\partial\Omega,
\end{array}\right. \end{equation} where $\Omega$ is a bounded domain in $R^{N}$, $N\geq2$, $\mu>0$, $\alpha\in(0,1)$, and $\Omega_{\mu}$ is a small subdomain of $\Omega$. We consider the case where $p>N$, and our analysis includes the application of the comparison principle and the application of the degree theory.
